### Identity Service REST API Client
@identityPort = 8080
@baseUrl = http://localhost:{{identityPort}}
@kongUrl = http://localhost:8000
@api = {{kongUrl}}/api/v1
@email = identity-demo@example.test
@password = SecurePassword123!
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@accessToken = paste-access-token-here

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

### JWKS Public Keys
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/jwks.json
Accept: application/json

### Register New User
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ssdsds@gmail.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "fullName": "Nguyen Van A"
}



### Login
# The response handler stores the token for the protected requests below.
# If the client does not support response handlers, copy data.accessToken to @accessToken.
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ssdsds@gmail.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

# > {%
#  client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.data.accessToken);
# %}


### Refresh Access Token
# The HTTP client retains the HttpOnly refresh_token cookie from login.
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh


### Get Current User Directly
# Kong normally derives this header from the Bearer JWT. Use it only for direct Identity calls.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
X-User-Id: {{userId}}
Accept: application/json

### Get Current User Through Kong
# Kong verifies the Bearer JWT via caller-context and injects x-user-id/x-user-roles.
GET {{kongUrl}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Update Current User Directly
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me
X-User-Id: {{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Updated Nguyen Van A"
}

### Logout
POST {{api}}/auth/logout

### Refresh After Logout (expected 401 INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN)
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh

### Additional RBAC and shipping-address requests
# Use rbac.http and shipping-addresses.http for the protected workflows.
